<Prose title="OpenClaw on Sabha: bring your OpenClaw bot to your team's chat" description="Bring the OpenClaw bot you already run into Sabha, the agent-native, open-source alternative to Slack. It connects over a WebSocket, so it needs no public address." label="INTEGRATION" heading="OpenClaw on Sabha">
  <img slot="mark" src="/_site/logos/openclaw-claw.svg" alt="OpenClaw" width="56" height="56" />
  <FeatureVideo slot="figure" name="bot" width={1280} height={720} label="An OpenClaw bot replying in a Sabha channel" />
  <p>Already running an <a href="https://openclaw.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="landing-link">OpenClaw</a> bot? Bring it into Sabha. It joins your workspace as a bot with its own name, key and permissions, in the channels you choose. People mention it, reply in its threads and react to it like any teammate.</p>

  <p>The bot connects out to Sabha over a WebSocket, so it needs no public address, webhook URL or tunnel. It can run on a laptop or on any server. It keeps your OpenClaw setup, skills and model keys, and Sabha never sees them. It works the same on sabha.co, on Sabha Cloud Deploy and on your own server.</p>

  <h3>Connect it</h3>

  <ol>
    <li>In <strong>Settings → Apps</strong>, add an app for the bot and put it in the channels it should answer in.</li>
    <li>On the app's <strong>API</strong> tab, choose <strong>OpenClaw</strong> under <strong>Set up with</strong>. The steps fill in your workspace's address and the bot's key.</li>
    <li>Paste them on the machine where OpenClaw runs. They install <code>@sabha-co/openclaw-sabha</code>, connect it, and restart the gateway. The <strong>API</strong> tab shows when the bot is online.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>What it can do</h3>

  <p>It answers when mentioned, replying in a thread, and keeps talking in any thread it's part of without another mention. It reads and sends files, reacts, edits its own messages, searches history and looks people up. Let people message it, and it answers direct messages too. An administrator decides what each bot's key may do.</p>

  <h3>Beside Sabha's agent</h3>

  <p>Sabha also has an agent built in, which answers from your company brain. Your OpenClaw bot works beside it, doing whatever you built it for.</p>

